hey this is presh talwalkar  team a has four girls and seven boys  team a takes five days to paint four  rooms  team b has seven girls and ten boys  team b takes four days to paint five  rooms  team c has eight girls and five boys  how long will it take team c to paint  six rooms  assume every girl works at a constant  rate every boy works at a constant rate  and every room is identical  this problem was posted to quora and  suggested to me by ole dele from nigeria  can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for a  solution  so let's set up some variables  let lowercase g be the percentage of a  room a girl paints daily  let capital g be the number of girls  working on a team  then capital g times lowercase g will be  the number of rooms that capital g girls  paint daily  we can set up similar variables for boys  let lowercase b equal the percentage of  a room a boy paints daily  let capital b equal the number of boys  working on a team then capital b times  lowercase b equals the number of rooms  capital b boys paint daily  now if we multiply  each of these by t days  we get the number of rooms that either g  girls or b boys paint in t days  now team a has four girls and seven boys  and it takes five days to paint four  rooms  so we add up the work that the girls do  and the work that the boys do to get a  total of four rooms  so this translates into the following  equation we have five times the quantity  four g plus five times the quantity  seven b is equal to 4.  5 times the quantity 4g is the amount of  work that the girls are doing and 5  times the quantity 7b is the amount of  work that the boys are doing to get a  total of 4 rooms  now for team b we can set up a similar  equation  we have four times the quantity seven g  plus four times the quantity ten b  equals five  now for team c  we know the number of girls and the  number of boys and we know that there  are six rooms and we want to solve for  the variable t  so we have t times the quantity 8g plus  5b equals 6.  so how can we solve for t  well let's take a look at the first two  equations we set up  we can rewrite the first equation as 20g  plus 35b equals four  the second equation becomes 28g plus 40b  is equal to 5.  now if we subtract the first equation  from the second we get eight g plus five  b is equal to one  and that exactly matches what we want to  find in team c  so just algebraically if we multiply  both sides by 6 we can see that t has to  be equal to 6.  we can also interpret the answer  if 8g plus 5b is equal to 1 that means 8  girls and 5 boys can paint one room in  one day  therefore it will take six days for team  c to paint six rooms  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math you can catch me on my blog mind  your decisions if you like this video  you can check out my books which are  listed in the video description and you  can support me on patreon if you have a  math topic you can email me presh  mindyourdecisions.com and you can catch  me on social media either at mind your  decisions or at presh tallwalker
 

